                                    <h1>Jewelry D2C Agency Contract &amp;mdash; Deliverables + KPIs + SLAs Essentials (2026) | ITD GrowthLabs</h1>
                                    <div style="background:#fff7ed;border-left:4px solid #ff5722;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:10px;margin:24px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;"><strong style="color:#ea580c;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:0.4px;">ITD JEWELRY PORTFOLIO &mdash; THE EVIDENCE:</strong><br>This article is written from live jewelry vertical work. ITD GrowthLabs is a specialist <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-jewelry-brands.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">digital marketing agency for jewelry brands</a> with a delivered <a href="/resources/Fabelia_Jewelry_D2C_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Fabelia jewelry D2C case study</a>, 8+ published jewelry playbooks including <a href="/resources/Gold_vs_Diamond_Jewelry_D2C_Strategy_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Gold vs Diamond D2C Strategy</a>, <a href="/resources/Jewelry_D2C_Digital_Transformation_India_Dubai_2026.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jewelry D2C Digital Transformation India + Dubai</a>, <a href="/resources/Best_D2C_Jewellery_Brands_UAE_GCC_2026_2027.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Best D2C Jewellery Brands UAE + GCC</a>, and city-specific jewelry marketing pages across <a href="/services/gcc/dubai-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dubai</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/abu-dhabi-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Abu Dhabi</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/jeddah-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Jeddah</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/doha-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Doha</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/dammam-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Dammam</a>, and <a href="/services/gcc/al-khobar-jewellery-agency.php" style="color:#ea580c;font-weight:700;">Al Khobar</a>. Every framework below is grounded in live category work &mdash; not generic D2C theory.</div><p>The agency contract is where jewelry founders either protect themselves or set up a 6-12 month painful engagement. Vague deliverables + soft SLAs + bundled ad spend + weak exit clauses cost 3-5x more than any legal-review investment. This piece walks through the 10 essential contract terms every jewelry founder must negotiate before signing.</p>
                                    <h2>The 10 essential contract terms</h2>
                                    <p><strong>1. Deliverables specificity + monthly quantification.</strong></p><p>"Marketing services" is not a deliverable. Specify: X paid channels managed, Y content pieces / month, Z blog articles, N Reels, monthly QBR, weekly reporting. Quantify everything.</p><p><strong>2. KPIs + measurement methodology.</strong></p><p>What metrics matter + how measured + who owns the source-of-truth. Ad spend + CPL + conversions from Google + Meta + Instagram + WhatsApp + organic + referrals + closed-won revenue tied via CRM. Weekly + monthly cadence + report format.</p><p><strong>3. SLA on issue resolution + escalation.</strong></p><p>Critical bugs / creative issues: 24-48 hours. Standard requests: 3-5 business days. Escalation path: junior &rarr; strategist &rarr; founder within contracted response time.</p><p><strong>4. Ad spend billing transparency (no markup).</strong></p><p>Contract explicitly states: ad spend transparent pass-through (Option A client pays platforms directly / Option B agency bills exactly what was spent with monthly attribution). No markup ever. Any exception requires written amendment.</p><p><strong>5. IP ownership + transfer clauses.</strong></p><p>Creative + content + Shopify + landing pages + email templates + brand guidelines &mdash; all owned by client. Agency has usage rights during engagement. Full IP + source files transferred at end of engagement or on request.</p><p><strong>6. Team commitments + no-swap without approval.</strong></p><p>Named team + LinkedIn accessible + founder-strategist involvement documented. No unauthorised team swaps mid-engagement without founder approval + 30-day notice.</p><p><strong>7. Exit clauses + notice period + milestone-based cancellation.</strong></p><p>Standard 6-month MSA with month-to-month cancellation after month 3 if agreed milestones missed. 30-day notice standard. No early-termination penalty if agency missed milestones.</p><p><strong>8. Data + platform access ownership.</strong></p><p>Meta Business Manager + Google Ads + Shopify + WhatsApp Cloud API + CRM + all analytics must be in client's account (not agency-owned). Agency has access during engagement. Access revoked at exit.</p><p><strong>9. Confidentiality + NDA.</strong></p><p>Mutual NDA covering business strategy + revenue data + customer data + creative concepts + roadmap. Standard 2-3 year post-engagement confidentiality.</p><p><strong>10. Payment terms + invoicing cadence.</strong></p><p>Retainer billed monthly in advance. Ad spend billed at end of month (Option B) or paid directly (Option A). Payment terms 15-30 days. Late-payment interest defined. Invoice format + GST compliance specified.</p>
                                    <h2>Standard MSA structure</h2>
                                    <p>A serious jewelry-agency Master Service Agreement (MSA) typically covers:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Recital + parties + effective date + term:</strong> Standard opening. Term typically 6-12 months.</li><li><strong>Scope of services + Statement of Work (SOW):</strong> Detailed deliverables per tier + monthly quantification + KPIs.</li><li><strong>Fees + payment terms:</strong> Retainer + ad-spend billing + one-time fees + payment schedule + invoice format.</li><li><strong>IP + ownership + license:</strong> Creative + content + platform-access ownership rights + transfer clauses.</li><li><strong>Confidentiality + NDA:</strong> Mutual obligations + post-engagement confidentiality period.</li><li><strong>Warranties + representations:</strong> Both parties confirm authority + accuracy of information + compliance with laws.</li><li><strong>Term + termination + exit:</strong> Notice periods + milestone-based cancellation + data + platform-access transfer at exit.</li><li><strong>Indemnification + liability limits:</strong> Standard mutual indemnity + agency liability capped at 6-12 months of retainer.</li><li><strong>Governing law + jurisdiction:</strong> Typically India (client's state) or Singapore for international brands.</li><li><strong>Dispute resolution + arbitration:</strong> Escalation path + mediation + arbitration if unresolved.</li></ul>
                                    <h2>Statement of Work (SOW) structure</h2>
                                    <p>SOW is the operational annexure to the MSA specifying:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Engagement tier + duration:</strong> Starter / Growth / Enterprise + 6-month or 12-month term.</li><li><strong>Monthly deliverables specifics:</strong> X paid channels, Y content pieces, Z blog articles, N Reels, monthly QBR, weekly reporting format.</li><li><strong>KPIs + measurement methodology:</strong> Metric definitions + measurement source-of-truth + reporting cadence + review milestones (30-day, 90-day, 6-month).</li><li><strong>Team + roles:</strong> Named team members + roles + escalation path + founder-strategist involvement.</li><li><strong>Milestone-based accountability:</strong> 30-day, 90-day, 6-month milestones tied to KPIs. Missing 90-day milestone triggers month-to-month cancellation right.</li><li><strong>Ad spend budget + approval process:</strong> Monthly ad-spend budget + client approval process for budget changes + performance-based reallocation authority.</li><li><strong>Change management:</strong> Process for adding / removing services + fee adjustments + written amendment requirement.</li></ul><p>Well-drafted SOW prevents 80% of client-agency disputes. Invest in legal review + specific-language SOW upfront.</p>
                                    <h2>Red flags in agency contract proposals</h2>
                                    <p>Watch for these red flags during contract negotiation:</p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Auto-renewal without notice:</strong> Contract auto-renews 12-month without written cancellation. Insist on explicit renewal (opt-in, not opt-out).</li><li><strong>Bundled ad-spend + retainer:</strong> Almost always hides 15-30% ad-spend markup. Insist on transparent pass-through.</li><li><strong>Vague deliverables:</strong> "Marketing services" or "content as needed". Insist on quantified monthly deliverables.</li><li><strong>Agency-owned platform accounts:</strong> Meta Business Manager or Google Ads in agency name = data lock-in. Insist on client-owned accounts.</li><li><strong>Weak IP + creative-ownership language:</strong> Agency retains ownership of creative + content. Insist on client ownership with agency usage rights during engagement.</li><li><strong>Long notice periods without milestone escape:</strong> 90-180 day notice + no milestone-based cancellation = 6-12 month lock-in even if agency fails. Insist on 30-day notice + milestone-based cancellation after month 3-6.</li><li><strong>Broad indemnification of agency:</strong> Client indemnifies agency for everything. Should be mutual + capped.</li><li><strong>Missing data + platform access transfer at exit:</strong> Contract silent on what happens to Meta + Google + Shopify + CRM access at exit. Insist on explicit transfer clause.</li></ul>
                                    <h2>Legal review + negotiation process</h2>
                                    <p>Recommended process:</p><ol style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Agency sends MSA + SOW draft after discovery + proposal.</li><li>Founder reviews with corporate lawyer (Rs 15-40K legal-review cost is well-invested).</li><li>Redline agreed changes + counter-proposal on ambiguous language + red flags.</li><li>Agency responds with revised draft. 2-3 rounds typical for well-drafted MSA.</li><li>Both parties sign. E-sign via DocuSign + attach SOW + payment schedule.</li><li>Kick-off meeting to confirm operational understanding + escalation path.</li></ol><p>Total negotiation timeline: 1-3 weeks. Rushed contracts + skipped legal review are false economies &mdash; they cost 3-10x during engagement or exit disputes.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
                                        <p style="color:#ccc;margin-bottom:25px;">Book a free 30-minute jewelry D2C discovery call. We map your brand + funnel + share a customised proposal within 3 working days.</p>
                                        <a href="https://www.itdgrowthlabs.com/contact-us.php" style="background:#ff5722;color:#fff;padding:14px 32px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block;margin-right:10px;">Contact Us Today</a>
